+# Design
+
+## Approach
+
+- Replace the public review's nested customer DTO with a minimal reviewer projection containing only first name, while retaining the existing review fields.
+- Add bean validation and explicit controller checks for integer rating range, authenticated customer identity, and duplicate reviews. Use Spring response statuses rather than translating expected client errors into 5xx responses.
+- Make merchant update/delete lookup product-scoped and keep the existing merchant/private routing for moderation.
+- Centralize aggregate recalculation in `ProductReviewServiceImpl`: load all reviews for the product after the mutation, sum ratings with `BigDecimal`, divide to scale 1 using `RoundingMode.HALF_UP`, and set zero values for an empty set. Ensure update preserves the existing entity and delete recalculates after removal.
+- Add focused controller/service/integration coverage for privacy, status codes, no-persistence rejection, moderation scoping, and aggregate transitions.
+
+## Compatibility
+
+The public review JSON intentionally becomes narrower to prevent personal-data leakage. Existing review id/rating/description/date fields remain available; the reviewer representation is reduced to first name.
+
+## Error Handling
+
+Expected validation, authorization, conflict, and not-found outcomes are returned directly as 400/403/409/404. Unexpected persistence or conversion failures remain server errors and must not partially persist a rejected request.
