+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Product reviews currently expose customer data that must remain private and return incorrect server errors for invalid or duplicate submissions. Product aggregates also become stale after moderation changes, so the public API can show misleading ratings.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Restrict public review responses to review id, rating, description, date, and reviewer first name.
+- Validate customer review ratings as integer values from 1 through 5 and return HTTP 400 for invalid values.
+- Enforce one review per customer and product with HTTP 409 for duplicates and HTTP 403 when the submitted customer does not match the authenticated customer.
+- Return HTTP 404 when merchants update or delete a missing review or a review belonging to another product.
+- Recalculate product average rating and count from persisted reviews after create, update, and delete, rounding averages to one decimal place using half-up rounding and returning zeroes when no reviews remain.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `product-reviews`: Public review privacy, customer submission rules, merchant moderation, and product rating aggregates.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+Affected v1 review controllers, review DTOs/populators, product review persistence services, product response mapping, and API/integration tests. No new external dependency is required.
